   "before": "**Failure envelopes carry their errors.** A `kind=failure` envelope requires a\nnonempty `errors` array of `DomainDetail`; where a step termination's optional\n`domainDetail` is absent, the composition in native \u00a710 supplies the array from\nthe route's own detail code, and where it is present `errors` is exactly that\ndetail so the two surfaces never disagree. Before a Plan or Run exists no run\nenvelope is fabricated. A failure golden (request-rejected or operational-failed) carries its\nactual `domainDetail`; only a golden whose `detailSuppliedBy` names that composition may omit\nit. An unsupported envelope major is `REQUEST.SCHEMA_MAJOR_UNSUPPORTED` with\n`OUTPUT.ENVELOPE_MAJOR_UNSUPPORTED`; an empty latest resolver is `IDENTITY.UNKNOWN` with the\nquery owner's `QUERY.VIEW_UNKNOWN`.",
   "after": "**Failure envelopes carry their errors.** A `kind=failure` envelope requires an\n`errors` array of `DomainDetail`. Normally it is nonempty: where a step\ntermination's optional `domainDetail` is absent, the composition in native \u00a710\nsupplies the array from the route's own detail code, and where it is present\n`errors` is exactly that detail so the two surfaces never disagree. Two closed\nexceptions use `errors=[]`: the selected metadata successor's\n`REQUEST.UNKNOWN_OPTION` form with its required diagnostic, and the selected\nenvelope6 interruption form when this invocation has no earlier committed\nRun, including a Run from an optional analysis/verify step. The interruption form carries only the existing interrupted\nclass, owned signal and exit130, without an invented detail or result. The host\nmust perform the appropriate private host join before selecting it. Before\nplanning, `J-INTERRUPTION-PREPLANNING` compares the reserved host RequestContext\nand its observed signal with the new empty failure, without fabricating an\ninvocation or step. After planning, `J-INTERRUPTION-LEDGER` joins RequestId and\noptional correlation fields to the admitted, finalized invocation, requires\nrecorded before-settle cancellation with matching step signals, and preserves\nthe last completed analysis/verify Run from any earlier step, including an\noptional step. Required steps alone still determine settled D9 aggregation and\nsettlement phase. Cancelled steps have no result, carry the matching interrupted\ntermination, and every subsequent step is cancelled. Result kinds match their\nstep kinds (analysis/verify both use AnalysisResult). A Run-bearing output names\nthe exact admitted Run result, or carries the exact invocation ledger. With no\ncommitted Run, emit a failure or an exact invocation carrier; no findings or\nadvisoryReport payload is carried. Invocation-scoped availability follows the\nrelease-availability rule above even without a committed Run. Every before-settle\ninterrupted carrier (failure, run or invocation) projects the complete\nin-step-order list of recorded domainDetails on earlier request-rejected or\noperational-failed steps, including optional steps and excluding skipped or\ncancelled steps. A nonempty list is always carried as errors, exactly. For an\nempty list, failure carries errors:[] while run/invocation omit errors, matching\nthe existing shape constraint. There is no host choice between these forms.\nNo changed remedies, duplicates, omissions or invented entries are\nadmitted. At step recording, for every rejected or operationally failed step,\nthe host persists its actual composed route detail in that step's existing\noptional domainDetail; this duty applies even if no interruption later occurs.\nAbsence of a saved detail never authorizes a renderer to invent one.\nDo not manufacture\na query/doctor completion or an unrelated current error detail. A Run selected as a query input is not a Run committed by an\nearlier step of this invocation. Cancellation after settlement cannot select\nthis form or reclassify the settled aggregate. The original step outcomes remain\nin the invocation ledger. This semantic join is a host duty; envelope shape\nalone cannot prove ledger custody or absence of a committed Run. Before a Plan or Run exists no run\nenvelope is fabricated. A failure golden (request-rejected or operational-failed) carries its\nactual `domainDetail`; only a golden whose `detailSuppliedBy` names that composition may omit\nit. An unsupported envelope major is `REQUEST.SCHEMA_MAJOR_UNSUPPORTED` with\n`OUTPUT.ENVELOPE_MAJOR_UNSUPPORTED`; an empty latest resolver is `IDENTITY.UNKNOWN` with the\nquery owner's `QUERY.VIEW_UNKNOWN`."
